Valid values: 1 to 24.

Default value: 6.', example='6', position='Query'),
  MFAOperationForLogin?: string(name='MFAOperationForLogin', description='Specifies the MFA policy for user logon. This parameter replaces `EnforceMFAForLogin`. We recommend that you use this parameter. `EnforceMFAForLogin` is still valid. Valid values:

- `mandatory`: enforces MFA for all RAM users. This is equivalent to setting `EnforceMFAForLogin` to `true`.

- `independent` (default): The MFA settings for each RAM user are not affected. This is equivalent to setting `EnforceMFAForLogin` to `false`.

- `adaptive`: enforces MFA only for unusual logons.', example='adaptive', position='Query'),
  maxIdleDaysForAccessKeys?: int32(name='MaxIdleDaysForAccessKeys', description='The maximum idle period of the AccessKey pairs of RAM users. An AccessKey pair that is not used for the specified period of time is automatically disabled on the next day. You can set the value to one of the following numbers:

- 90

- 180

- 365

- 730 (default)', example='365', position='Query'),
  maxIdleDaysForUsers?: int32(name='MaxIdleDaysForUsers', description='The maximum idle period of RAM users. If a RAM user who can log on to the console does not log on to the console for the specified period of time (SSO logons are not included), the console logon feature of the RAM user is disabled on the next day. You can set the value to one of the following numbers:

- 90

- 180

- 365

- 730 (default)', example='365', position='Query'),
  operationForRiskLogin?: string(name='OperationForRiskLogin', description='This parameter is deprecated.', example='autonomous', deprecated='true', position='Query'),
  verificationTypes?: [ string ](name='VerificationTypes', description='The MFA methods.', shrink='json', position='Query'),
}

